id: pm-graph-b3sw
title: "pm-graph status help documents the version field with a stale literal, and the release version-bump regex targets that string instead of the real declaration"
description: "The status command's help output map describes every field except version, which carries the literal 2026.7.28 rather than a description. The release workflow's first version regex is unanchored and non-global, so in this package its only match is that nested help string; the authoritative declarations are manifest.json and the EXTENSION_VERSION constant. Fixing the help text alone would be silently undone on the next release, so the regex must be anchored to the manifest property level in the same change."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:help-output","area:release-automation"
created_at: "2026-07-29T22:24:17.487Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T22:32:37.806Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T22:32:37.796Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T22:32:37.796Z"
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "The status help output documents version as a field description, not as a version literal; The release version-bump regex cannot match a nested string, so the help text survives a release; A test fails if the status help version entry ever becomes version-like again"
risk: low
confidence: high
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T22:32:37.440Z",codex,"Both guard tests were verified by reintroducing each bug and confirming failure, then restoring: the help-text assertion fails when version carries a literal, and the release-regex assertion fails when the pattern is un-anchored. release:check green with 195 tests and coverage 83.20/78.47/89.66 against thresholds 81/77/88."
close_reason: "Help output now documents the version field as a description, and the release rewrite is anchored to the manifest property level so it cannot restamp a nested string. Both halves are guarded by tests proven to fail on the reintroduced bug."
